              <summary><h3>Can protein powder harm my baby?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  A plain, well-tested protein powder used in normal amounts is not known to harm a developing baby. Potential harm comes from what else may be in a product: lead and other heavy metals, caffeine, unstudied herbs and very high vitamin A. Choosing an independently tested product with a short ingredient list addresses nearly all of those, and your OB can review the label with you.
                </p>
