                  Yes, commercial whey is made from pasteurized milk and is an ordinary dairy protein, so it is generally considered safe in pregnancy unless you have a cow's milk allergy. Whey isolates are low in lactose and tend to test lower for heavy metals than plant proteins. Choose a certified product such as Thorne or Klean Isolate and avoid whey blends with stimulants or herbs.
